    ['coupled-growth','Coupled eutectic growth','growth front;solute redistribution','Simultaneous growth of adjacent α and β at a shared front; each phase rejects solute needed by its neighbor, allowing short-range liquid diffusion.','','Two solids formed separately from a solid solution are not necessarily a eutectic constituent.','eutectic;precipitation;interlamellar-spacing','5–13'],
    ['interlamellar-spacing','Interlamellar spacing','λ;lambda;lamellar spacing','The repeat spacing of neighboring lamellae; faster regular eutectic growth generally gives finer spacing and greater strength.','λ = cR^(−1/2), equivalently λ²R = c²; R = growth rate, c = system-dependent constant.','Doubling R divides λ by √2; colony size is a separate measure.','coupled-growth;colony','11–13'],
    ['strain-hardening','Strain hardening','work hardening;cold working;cold-work','Strengthening by plastic deformation that raises dislocation density and their mutual resistance to movement.','','It is distinct from solute strengthening, particle strengthening and aging heat treatments.','dislocation;hot-working;dispersion-strengthening','3, 11'],
    ['grain-refinement','Grain refinement','grain-size strengthening;Hall–Petch','Reducing grain size to increase boundary obstacles to slip; finer prior austenite also supplies more pearlite nucleation sites.','Common trend: σ_y = σ_0 + k_y d^(−1/2), with grain size d (background relation).','Grain or colony size is not interlamellar spacing.','grain-boundary;colony;interlamellar-spacing','3, 11'],
    ['nonequilibrium-eutectic','Nonequilibrium eutectic','interdendritic eutectic','Eutectic that forms from enriched residual liquid during rapid freezing, even if the nominal alloy would finish freezing as one phase in equilibrium.','','Later β precipitation below the solvus starts from solid α and does not require residual liquid.','precipitation;microsegregation;incipient-melting','16–17'],
    ['soldering','Soldering','solder;casting alloy','Joining using a lower-melting filler; eutectic systems offer low melting temperatures useful for soldering and casting.','','Eutectic reactions also occur in ceramic systems, not only metals.','eutectic-point;solidification','14–15']
